 "notes": "The southern tip of Bonaire: entry over the ironshore between the southernmost slave huts, a sandbar and shallow reef at 3-12 m where rays feed, soft-coral fields cut by sand channels to about 25 m and a steep drop-off to 40 m and more, with a chain leading to a field of old ship anchors from about 45 m (bonaire.com, divers-guide.com, infobonaire.com). The current is strong and changes direction within minutes; a southerly current carries divers away from the reef, so the route turns north first. Hut positions from OpenStreetMap; zone widths are approximate; the anchors are placed straight out from the entry because their exact spot is not published, and the route is illustrative. Coastline, pier and dive-site markers © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL). Positions are approximate.",
